<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea wage growth slows to 11.6 pct in first qtr.</title>
<headline>S.Korea wage growth slows to 11.6 pct in first qtr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average wage increase in South Korea slowed to 11.6 percent year-on-year in the first quarter of this year against a 13.7 percent rise a year earlier, the Labour Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The average wage during the period totalled 1.43 million won from 1.28 million a year ago, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>It said the work week dropped to 45.5 hours in the first quarter from 46.4 a year earlier because of reduced overtime.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
